  "clf_control": {
   "text": "\"<<The Choke of the River>>  \nThe Pocomoke flows with a rhythm of old,  \nIts waters deep and dark, a secret told.  \nFish swim in circles, lost in the current's dance,  \nWhile the river's voice echoes through the land.  \n\nThe sun sets low, casting long shadows wide,  \nAnd the river's song grows louder, more fierce.  \nIt carries the weight of forgotten dreams,  \nAnd the stories of those who once were.  \n\nThe banks are lined with willows, swaying low,  \nTheir leaves whispering tales of what was.  \nThe river's heart beats with a steady tune,  \nA reminder of the life that once was.  \n\nBut sometimes, the current turns, and it's dark,  \nA deep, dark current that takes what it's given.  \nThe river's voice grows cold, a warning in song,  \nOf the dangers that lie beneath its flowing song.  \n\nSo here I stand, on the edge of the stream,  \nWatching the river's journey, its fate unknown.  \nIt's a tale of loss, of change, of time,  \nAnd the river's song will never be the same.",
